  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia Protracted Crisis Joint Response 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aid implementation happens in the sectors FSL, WASH, Health, Nutrition and MPC.
In the FSL sector, agricultural support is provided to reduce food insecurity, as well as food assistance. SOMJR 2022-2023 will see the continuation and expansion of the construction and rehabilitation of sustainable water sources and of latrines. With hygiene and sanitation promotion activities, emphasizing on IDP in camps. In the health sector, facilities are supported with finances and resources. In regards to nutrition, Community Management of Acute Malnutrition takes place in 14 places as wel as the scaling up of routine screening cases. Protection is promoted through activities like awareness campaigns. Finally, MPC transfers is provided to households.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target communities for the SOMJR 2022-2023 include, urban, agropastoral and pastoral communities. They are affected by conflict/violence, drought, desert locust and the health and socio-economic impacts of the COVID-19 pandemic. SOMJR members will target communities where IPC3 and above conditions 
prevail. The focus in the programme is both on vulnerable IDPs and host communities. Some livelihood activities will specifically target women.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The World Vision programming focuses on FSL, WASH, Health and Multi-Purpose Cash.</narrative>
  </description>
